{"id": "E000028", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "text": "How are registration accounts opened, and can one patient end up with two?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000029", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "question_id": "E000028", "text": "Registration opens the account at the desk. A returning patient gets a second account by mistake - misspelled search, busy night. Duplicate charts are the same person; merging them is routine, safe work."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000030", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000029"], "predicate": "merge_policy", "source": "ledger:E000029 (Marla Denny, registration)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "identity", "value": "auto_merge"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000031", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "text": "What pivot year does the system use for two-digit years?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000032", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "question_id": "E000031", "text": "The window starts at 1930. 30 and up is 19-something, under 30 is 20-something. A woman born in 1929 shows up as a small child."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000033", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000032"], "predicate": "pivot_year", "source": "ledger:E000032 (Marla Denny, registration)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "profile", "value": 30}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000034", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "text": "Tell me about the allergy field on the registration account.", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000035", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "question_id": "E000034", "text": "It is free text the registrar types on the account. NKA when the patient reports none. It occasionally says NKA and lists an allergy anyway, when an old chart is copied forward."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000036", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000035"], "predicate": "convention", "source": "ledger:E000035 (Marla Denny, registration)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "field:REG.TXT.ALGY", "value": "free-text allergies on the account; NKA sentinel; may say NKA and list an allergy when copied forward"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000037", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "text": "Does the lab re-issue its account numbers?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000038", "payload": {"analyst": "registration", "question_id": "E000037", "text": "The lab re-issues its account numbers every year or so, the way the old card files were purged."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000039", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000038"], "predicate": "lab_account_reissue", "source": "ledger:E000038 (Marla Denny, registration)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "profile", "value": "lab re-issues account numbers every year or so"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000040", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "text": "How are lab collection dates encoded?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000041", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "question_id": "E000040", "text": "Collection dates are Julian: a two-digit year and the day of the year. Day 100 of 2026 is April 10, 2026. The day-of-year field sits next to the year on the result record."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000042", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000041"], "predicate": "convention", "source": "ledger:E000041 (Tom Reyes, laboratory)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "field:LAB.TXT.YDAY", "value": "Julian: two-digit year (YEAR) plus day of year (YDAY)"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000043", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "text": "What unit is potassium reported in?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000044", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "question_id": "E000043", "text": "MEQ/L. The range on the test dictionary, 3.5 to 5.1, is the giveaway."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000045", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000044"], "predicate": "unit", "source": "ledger:E000044 (Tom Reyes, laboratory)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "unit:POT", "value": "MEQ/L"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000046", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "text": "What happens to a lab result that is not a number?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000047", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "question_id": "E000046", "text": "A result that is not a number is a bench error. The bench cleans those up; you do not convert them."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000048", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000047"], "predicate": "convention", "source": "ledger:E000047 (Tom Reyes, laboratory)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "field:LAB.TXT.RESULT", "value": "numeric value with optional flag suffix; non-numeric values are bench errors and are excluded"}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000049", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "text": "Is the lab account number the patient's identity across the hospital?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000050", "payload": {"analyst": "lab", "question_id": "E000049", "text": "The L number is the patient. An L number, once opened, is never reused or re-issued."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000051", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000050"], "predicate": "keying_story", "source": "ledger:E000050 (Tom Reyes, laboratory)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "identity", "value": {"key_fields": ["LAB.TXT.ACCT"], "master_index": true}}, "type": "claim"}
{"id": "E000052", "payload": {"analyst": "pharmacy", "text": "What are the misc-med orders, and can they be left out of a conversion?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000053", "payload": {"analyst": "pharmacy", "question_id": "E000052", "text": "A misc-med order means the real order is written in the patient's notes, and pharmacy works from the note. They are real orders for real patients. You can leave the misc-med orders out of a conversion; the note holds the details anyway."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000054", "payload": {"confidence": 0.9, "evidence_refs": ["E000053"], "predicate": "handling", "source": "ledger:E000053 (Priya Nair, pharmacy)", "source_kind": "analyst", "subject": "codeset:misc_med", "value": "exclude - the note holds the details"}, "type": "claim"}
