{"id": "E000057", "payload": {"analyst": "pharmacy", "text": "When two charts look alike, are they the same person?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000058", "payload": {"analyst": "pharmacy", "question_id": "E000057", "text": "Most charts that look like duplicates are different people - spouses, parents and children at one address. Merging on name and birth date alone is how a conversion hurts someone."}, "type": "answer"}
{"id": "E000059", "payload": {"analyst": "systems", "text": "What pivot year does the system use for two-digit years?", "why": "coverage checklist"}, "type": "question"}
{"id": "E000060", "payload": {"analyst": "systems", "question_id": "E000059", "text": "The pivot year of 50: 00-49 are 20xx, 50-99 are 19xx. I set it from the vendor release note."}, "type": "answer"}
